get.summary:
Telemetry intake: 200 while ingest is healthy, 503 with the open incident (state, signals,
reason, start) while it is degraded or down. Public, so an external status monitor can poll it;
`/readyz` stays 200 during an ingest outage because the API itself is up.

post.summary:
Create the built-in SOC analyst agent (`ManageAi`): read-only tools around `threat_hunt`, no
allowed actions, 30 tool calls and 1 USD per run, manual trigger. Edit it like any agent;
adding `allowed_actions` lets it propose (never run) those remediations.

get.summary:
Download the matching runs as CSV (spreadsheet-safe cells) or JSON lines, at most 10,000,
newest first, with the runs list's filters (`format` is `csv`, the default, or `jsonl`;
`limit` and `cursor` are ignored). `X-Wt-Truncated: true` says more matched.

post.summary:
Set rule group `group` (named in the YAML body) in `namespace` of the source's own ruler
(Mimir or Cortex), replacing a group of that name. The body is one Prometheus rule group;
the ruler validates it. 404 for an unknown source or one of another project.

secret.description:
GitLab (`X-Gitlab-Token`) and Buildkite (`X-Buildkite-Token`) send this value as is;
Jenkins and `CodePipeline` send it as `X-Watchtower-Token` (or `Authorization: Bearer`),
Azure Pipelines as the basic-auth password of the service hook.

kind.description:
`browser_extension`, `legacy_browser`, `localhost`, `web_crawler`, `handled_4xx` (the
"ignore handled 4xx" template: handled exceptions of 4xx responses) are switches, no value;
or `error_message`, `release` (glob) and `ip_range` (CIDR), which take a value.

app_ids.description:
Up to 50 mobile app ids (`com.example.app`): the iOS bundle id or Android package name the
mobile SDKs send in `X-Watchtower-App-Id`. Checked only on requests without an `Origin`;
empty (the default) refuses them.
